<Layout
  title={"RCE Compile: A Law of Compilation, Tested as a Normal Form Against Real Compilers"}
  description={"About: RCE Compile asks whether one statement of what compilation is holds for any compiler, independent of the Reality Code Engine. It fails as a description and holds as a normal form with two bounds and a measured distance from them."}
>
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">Research study · draft · about</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight">
      RCE Compile: A Law of Compilation, Tested as a Normal Form Against Real Compilers
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      RCE Compile is a research project in the repository of the Reality Code Engine (RCE). It asks whether one statement of what compilation is, a Law of Compilation, holds for any compiler, independent of RCE. Checked against twelve families of production compilers, the candidate fails as a description: no compiler hashes a name-free representation, lowering in shipping compilers is neither total nor proved to preserve meaning, and no compiler accounts for energy. It holds as a normative framework: a normal form with two bounds and a measured distance from them, against which every compiler can be placed.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray mb-3">What the study claims and what it does not</p>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <li>It claims that the candidate, as first stated, is falsified as a description of real compilers, and gives the evidence part by part.</li>
        <li>It states a refined standard with seven parts, four equivalence levels and a gate that names what it preserves, and seven hypotheses with falsifiers.</li>
        <li>It does not claim a measured energy result, a measured 98/2 split, or priority over earlier work: two primary sources (Hoare, He and Sampaio, 1993; Ershov, 1977) have not yet been read in full, and almost every external source was seen only as a search result.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <figure class="mt-10 glass-card p-4 fig-wide">
      <a class="fig-zoom" href="/figures/rce-compile/form-evidence.svg" aria-label="Enlarge figure"><img src="/figures/rce-compile/form-evidence.svg" alt="Grid of twelve compiler families against the seven parts of the Compiler Form; energy is absent in every row." class="fig-img w-full rounded bg-white" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a>
      <figcaption class="mt-3 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">Where each part of the Compiler Form is found, by compiler family. Qualitative; almost every cell rests on search-result or memory evidence.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
